## Question 1
Why is the list in RideManager typed ArrayList<Ride> and not ArrayList<Jeepney>?
 
Your answer:Because Ride is the general class, so the list can store different types of rides that are subclasses of Ride, including Jeepney. If it was ArrayList<Jeepney>, it could only store Jeepney objects.
 
## Question 2
In showStudentDiscounts(), why must you check instanceof before the cast?
 
Your answer:We check instanceof first to make sure the object is really a StudentRide before casting it. This helps prevent errors or crashes if the object is a different type of Ride.




